 The existing type 11 copy-row counters are retained when they change, sampled
 by the frame writer every 250 ms, to report actual per-row blits separately.
 
+Linear heap shadows on Turnip keep their Metal-visible tight rows. For single-sample,
+single-level, single-layer 2D color images with 4, 8 or 16 bytes per texel and a
+row pitch that misses 64-byte alignment, the existing unsigned-integer view and
+compute copy write the original bits back in place. Unsupported views or dispatch
+ranges retain the copy path. Region bounds, independent-writer merges and image
+view ownership follow the existing shadow implementation. CPU Vulkan tests cover
+the remaining 1202 by 2610 BGRA shape, sRGB, wider words and copy fallbacks;
+performance on A840 awaits the candidate's hardware capture.
+
+The diagnostic operation budget is 2,097,152 records (144 MiB plus one exhaustion
+record), covering a longer sequence of glass and application animation tests.
+After exhaustion, frame, CPU-stage and copy-row summaries continue. The operation
+hook and its bound remain disabled when diagnostics are disabled.
+
